    <GaugingStation location="Quidenham" name="Wittle" number="33045">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound broad-crested weir gauging a Chalk catchment with large Boulder Clay overlay and predominantly arable land use. Flows are heavily affected by artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">No out of bank flow rating and weir known to drown during high flows which is not accounted for. Road embankment prevents bypassing. One rating applied across period of record. Theoretical rating modified by current meter measurements suitable to 0.64m.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound broad-crested weir (crest 3m), with central notch separated by splitter plates; situated under a road bridge.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Weir drowned in 1968 floods. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Flow regime altered by pumping of two boreholes into the river u/s of Quidenham to support Ely Ouse to Essex Transfer Scheme (abstraction point at Hockwold on the Little Ouse). This can lead to artifically raised flows during the summer. Other abstractions in the catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly Chalk largely overlain with Boulder Clay. Predominantly arable land.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">GI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Theoretical rating supported by gaugings up to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="AMAX3 beyond limit of confidence (0.64m) and no gaugings available to validate rating." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
